    <briefdescription>
<para>Thread-safe in-memory listener that records all received events. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Primarily intended for unit tests and integration tests. An optional callback is invoked synchronously (under the mutex) after each event is recorded.</para>
<para>Example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1metadata_1_1_recording_metadata_change_listener_1ab7505b39b7114add8c1f2de41a8e2600" kindref="member">RecordingMetadataChangeListener</ref><sp/>rec;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...<sp/>wire<sp/>rec<sp/>into<sp/>SchemaManager<sp/>/<sp/>CatalogExporter<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EXPECT_EQ(rec.eventCount(),<sp/>1);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EXPECT_EQ(rec.lastEvent()-&gt;change_type,<sp/><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1metadata_1afd7078e993135071573cd065ff801f2ea0af71b5d145bdefec7d0a4c3462d6d6b" kindref="member">MetadataChangeType::TABLE_CREATED</ref>);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
